{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/pulls/3743","id":3107005882,"node_id":"PR_kwDOACTItM65MSW6","html_url":"https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/pull/3743","diff_url":"https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/pull/3743.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/pull/3743.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/issues/3743","number":3743,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Handle massive values in Retry-After when calculating time to sleep for","user":{"login":"meeb","id":2459512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTk1MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2459512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb","html_url":"https://github.com/meeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The method `Retry.parse_retry_after(...)` will accept any integer returned by the remote server in the `Retry-After` header when the server returns a number of seconds to delay for rather than an HTTP-date. This includes massive and invalid values, for example `Retry-After: 9999999999`. This value is passed back to `Retry.sleep_for_retry(...)` which then uses the value directly in `time.sleep(...)`. The type is checked but not the value.\r\n\r\nUsing values for `time.sleep(...)` that exceed `PyTime_MAX` results in an OverflowError being raised:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>> time.sleep(9999999999)\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<python-input-3>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n    time.sleep(9999999999)\r\n    ~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\nOverflowError: timestamp too large to convert to C PyTime_t\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis minimal PR adds a sanity check to confirm that the value of the `Retry-After` header is < 2147483647 (2 ** 31 - 1) in value. While `PyTime_MAX` is a `INT64_MAX` this is still a relatively sane upper bound value. If the value exceeds 2147483647 a clearer and more descriptive exception is raised.\r\n\r\nThis issue was seen in the wild:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/meeb/whoisit/issues/60\r\n\r\nIt's highly unlikely that actually sleeping for decades or centuries is desirable but that's a different issue. I don't believe there's a specified sensible maximum for `Retry-After` in the RFC, perhaps limiting this to `3600` or similar lower value would be sensible?\r\n\r\nCurrently, even with this PR, a semi-malicious server could add `if ($http_user_agent ~ urllib3) { add_header retry-after 5000000000; }` and lock up some clients that attempt to handle retries properly for over a century (or at least until the process gets killed).","created_at":"2025-12-16T16:35:00Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T07:20:28Z","closed_at":"2025-12-29T17:41:42Z","merged_at":"2025-12-29T17:41:42Z","merge_commit_sha":"13f0bfd55e4468fe1ea9c6f809d3a87b0f93ebab","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/pulls/3743/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/pulls/3743/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/issues/3743/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urllib3/urllib3/statuses/6eab28002f6df1c66d799555d2aacbadb6bcdac1","head":{"label":"meeb:add-retry-after-value-check","ref":"add-retry-after-value-check","sha":"6eab28002f6df1c66d799555d2aacbadb6bcdac1","user":{"login":"meeb","id":2459512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTk1MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2459512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb","html_url":"https://github.com/meeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":null},"base":{"label":"urllib3:main","ref":"main","sha":"83f8643ffb5b7f197457379148e2fa118ab0fcdc","user":{"login":"urllib3","id":26825299,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2ODI1Mjk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26825299?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3","html_url":"https://github.com/urllib3","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urllib3/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin"